xpad version 1.3 README
-------------------------

xpad is a virtual sticky pad system using GTK+ 2.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
INSTALLATION NOTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
     To compile, just type "make" and / or "make install".

     Read the INSTALL file for more.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
USAGE NOTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Right click to obtain configuration options and open new pads.

     Closing a pad saves the contents for later.  Destroying one destroys
		the contents.

     Hold down CTRL and left-click drag to move a pad.  Hold down CTRL and 
		right-drag to resize a pad.

     Add xpad to your ~/.xinitrc to have xpad start with every X boot.

     xpad stores its files in ~/.xpad.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------
COMMAND ARGUMENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	Standard GTK+ arguments are understood.  In addition, the following
		arguments are available.

	--help:			Prints usage information and exits.

	--version:		Prints version information and exits.

	--verbosity=%i: 	Where %i is the amount of output you desire.
				0 is none; 1 is moderate; 2 is debug.  
				Default is 0
	
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
KNOWN BUGS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
	POSIX-centric.  Win32, if GTK+ 2 ran on it, doesn't work.
	Preferences don't apply across multiple simultaneous xpad processes.
	Windows will not let themselves be sizes smaller than longest word.
	Top text can disappear momentarily when text is being entered on the
		bottom of the pad.
	

